  "sections": [
    {
      "section_code": "thesis",
      "section_title": "Sector Synthesis & Thesis",
      "content": "The Indian Defence Sector is in the midst of a multi-year structural super-cycle driven by the government's aggressive\nIndigenisation Negative Import Lists\nand an ambitious defence export target of\n\u20b950,000 Cr by FY29\n. With combined order books exceeding\n\u20b93.82 Lakh Cr\n(4.8x book-to-bill), revenue visibility is guaranteed for the next 4 to 6 years.\nHowever, performance is bifurcating between\nsystem integrators with high ROH/service content\n(HAL, BEL, Mazagon Dock) which enjoy structurally higher OPMs (24%-29%), and\npure missile/ammunition assembly players\n(BDL) subject to import component choke points and inventory delays.",
      "source_locator": "defence-q1fy27-sector-review.html#.synth"
    }
  ],
